  <tr valign="bottom">
    <td colspan="11" align="left" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"><p><a href="index.htm">Home</a></p>
      <p><b>Table 1</b>. Sample size, length range
        (cm), length-weight parameter estimates (<i>a</i> and <i>b</i>) and the
        standard deviations (standard errors) of those estimates (<i>s</i><i><sub>a</sub></i> and <i>s</i><i><sub>b</sub></i>),
        standard error of the weight estimate (<i>s<sub>W</sub></i>), and regression
        correlation coefficient (<i>r</i><sup>2</sup>) for 74 fish species, by
        season or seasonal groups and by gender ("Unsexed" = gender not specified; "Combined" =
        unsexed, males, and females). (Species are ordered by NODC taxonomic code.)</p></td>
  </tr>
